From 201d4c6e1e673052678d82b62ab665299041bef4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:55:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-sync): a pull that only applied feed rows defers
 the full repair pass like a replica-cursor move [daveey]

On a primary board the pull applies other gateways' writes to this gateway's own cards (worker heartbeats,
claims) into the live file. The kanban_repair_* triggers moved the live revision, so the full repair pass
(repair_divergence, repair_missing_children, partition scans) ran on every pulling round: the MacBook sync
thread used 14-19% of a core with no gateway work (t_01a1a80b7d6cc910).

apply_remote_changes now reads kanban_repair_revision right after its write transaction begins and right
before it commits (ApplyResult.revision_before/after, None without the table). pull collects each apply's
pair (revisions=). _defer_repair credits a live revision change when the pairs chain without a gap from the
credited revision (last pass's, or the last deferring round's) to this round's; then it defers exactly like
the replica-cursor case (REPLICA_REPAIR_MIN_S, _REPAIR_DEFERRED, repair_deferred). Any gap (a local write
before, between or after the applies), a None revision or a rebuild (resync) repairs at once as before. A
completed pass and reset_board_watch clear the credit. The repair-window state moves to
kanban_sync_repair_window.py (re-exported) to keep kanban_sync_client.py under its line cap.
---
